These are model SQL errors, raised while dbt creates the tables. `schema.yml` for `stg_customers` and `stg_orders` only has column descriptions, and a bad test would be reported as a test failure after the model had already built. The SQL follows the PowerCenter source: `RAW_CUSTOMERS` is `ID, NAME` and `RAW_ORDERS` is `ID, CUSTOMER, ORDERED_AT, STORE_ID, SUBTOTAL, TAX_PAID, ORDER_TOTAL`. The jaffle shop seeds are `id, first_name, last_name` and `id, user_id, order_date, status`. Regenerating the YAML would leave the same `select`. Mapping those seed names onto the Informatica columns would hard-code jaffle shop, which the converter is not allowed to do.

